  "term": "hand–arm vibration syndrome",
  "definition": "Hand–arm vibration syndrome is an occupational condition caused by long-term exposure to vibration, usually in people who regularly use vibrating tools. It affects the fingers, hands, and forearms and can cause episodes of finger whitening, numbness, tingling, and reduced nerve sensitivity.",
